Z||000000||loafer87gt||04-26-2000||12:40 AM||||Hi guys, I have posted several times about the problems I have been having with my GT, about how it bucks and lurches like if you release the clutch with the too little gas, almost like the engine is cutting in and out. The dealership gave me back the car and it has only done it to me once since I got it back. The interesting thing is that my tach has quit working and occasionaly jumps around. I know this is related to the tach filter, but is there any chance that this could be causing my problems with the bucking as well? I am gonna trying pulling the Tach filter next time it acts up, this would be great if this solved the problem. What exactly does the tach filter do, and if it was faulty how would it affect my car besides the tach not working? thanks guys, I have my fingers crossed that this might fix it!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fret Naught||04-26-2000||01:00 AM||||Try searching the threads for tach filter, seems just last week there was quite a bit of discussion concerning it. As far as I know the only thing the tack filter does is filter the generated signal sent the the tach. It will be interesting to see what every one else has to say. By the way I noticed my 86 SE V6 doing the same thing tonight I just figured I was going to slow and trying to feather the clutch to much. I will pay closer attention tommrow.||||reg||1
